course: dictionary
lesson: 2686
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Diddle is one of them. Its meaning depends on the sentence around it, so the context tells you which meaning to use.
explain: «I've been diddled» means someone cheated you, often out of money in a sneaky way. «Stop diddling about» means stop wasting time and fiddling around. Read the clues: who is doing what, and why?
explain: In a nursery rhyme, the words can be nonsense. «Hey diddle diddle, the cat and the fiddle» is just silly fun for the sound of the words. Not every word has to make sense to be part of a rhyme.
fact: Diddle is an informal word, mostly used in the UK.
fact: To diddle someone means to cheat them, especially out of money, in a sneaky way.
fact: To diddle about means to waste time or fiddle with something instead of getting on with it.
fact: In «Hey diddle diddle», diddle is a nonsense sound that makes the rhyme fun to say.
fact: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have probably chosen the right meaning.
exercise: «I think the shopkeeper tried to diddle me out of my pocket money.» What does diddle mean here? | To sing a happy tune | *To cheat someone in a sneaky way | To grow very tall | To paint a picture
exercise: Lena says, «Stop diddling about and get your coat on!» What does diddling about mean? | Sleeping in a warm bed | *Wasting time, fiddling about | Shouting loudly at a friend | Running very fast
exercise: In «Hey diddle diddle, the cat and the fiddle», what is diddle? | A rude word | *A nonsense sound, with no real meaning | A name for a cat | A kind of slow music
test: Tom says, «I've been diddled. That shop charged me far too much.» What has happened to Tom? | He found a lost dog in the park | He won a prize in a shop | *He was cheated and charged too much | He was given a free ice cream
test: Why is it useful to notice when someone is diddling others? | Because it means they are funny | Because it means they are kind and generous | Because it means they are tired and need a nap | *Because it shows the person is being dishonest
exam: «Sam was diddling about instead of tidying his room, so his mum was cross.» What does diddling about mean? | Cleaning very quickly | Cheating his mum out of money | *Wasting time | Singing a rhyme
